      "id": "modulation-changing-key-mid-tune",
      "title": "Modulation: Changing Key Mid-Tune",
      "level": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Track:** harmony | **Difficulty:** 8/10 | **Time:** ~10 min"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Modulation establishes a new tonic, not merely touching foreign chords."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-moves",
      "title": "Common moves",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Up a whole step (G→A) for energy. To relative minor (G→Em). Pivot chord shared by two keys (C major = IV in G, I in C)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "detection",
      "title": "Detection",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Sustained new accidentals + cadence confirming new tonic = modulation. Single A7 in D = tonicisation; four bars in A with A cadence = modulation."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trad-context",
      "title": "Trad context",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Less common in core repertoire than céilí arrangements and song verses."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "entities": [],
  "entity_order": [],
